{"status":"success","data":[{"site":{"siteid":3102,"sitename":"Färskesjön","sitedescription":"Lake with rocky or sandy shore. Physiography: rocky hills and some moraine area. Surrounding vegetation: Quercus, Pinus, Fagus, Alnus-Rhamnus fen.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[15.86049,56.15907]}","altitude":11,"collectionunitid":3910,"collectionunit":null,"handle":"FARSKE","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/5sjg-nn53"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":12730,"ageyoung":66},{"units":"Radiocarbon years BP","ageold":10424,"ageyoung":81}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":4037,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"B.E.","contactid":1000,"firstname":"Björn E.","familyname":"Berglund","contactname":"Berglund, Björn E."}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Data contributed by Berglund Björn E.\r\nPollen diagram in publications starts at 290 cm. Depths in data sheet at 5 cm. Water depth is 285 cm. Lithology refers to the depths as shown in the pollen diagram.\r\n\r\nUpper section 0-590 cm is in pollen diagram I, lowest section is in pollen diagram VII.","recdatecreated":"2013-09-30T14:02:42"}]}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}